Now update `PathlandDevUiProcessor`:
- imports:
  ```java
  import dev.pathland.view.core.protocol.ProtocolCatalog;
  import io.quarkus.arc.deployment.AdditionalBeanBuildItem;
  import org.jboss.jandex.DotName;
  import jakarta.inject.Singleton;
  ```
  Wait, `jakarta.inject.Singleton` is in the deployment classpath? The deployment module depends on `quarkus-arc-deployment`, which brings `jakarta.inject-api`. Use `DotName.createSimple("jakarta.inject.Singleton")` to avoid import? Better import `jakarta.inject.Singleton`.
- Add pages and build-time data:
  ```java
  card.addPage(Page.webComponentPageBuilder().title("Wire").icon("font-awesome-solid:code").componentLink("qwc-pathland-wire.js"));
  card.addPage(Page.webComponentPageBuilder().title("SSR").icon("font-awesome-solid:file-code").componentLink("qwc-pathland-ssr.js"));
  card.addPage(Page.webComponentPageBuilder().title("Protocol").icon("font-awesome-solid:book").componentLink("qwc-pathland-protocol.js"));
  card.addBuildTimeData("protocol", ProtocolCatalog.rows());
  ```
- Add bean registration:
  ```java
  @BuildStep(onlyIf = IsLocalDevelopment.class)
  AdditionalBeanBuildItem traceStore() {
      return AdditionalBeanBuildItem.builder()
              .addBeanClass(PathlandDevTraceStore.class)
              .setDefaultScope(DotName.createSimple(Singleton.class.getName()))
              .setUnremovable()
              .build();
  }
  ```
  Need import `PathlandDevTraceStore`.
- The `JsonRPCProvidersBuildItem` already registers the RPC; it injects the trace store.
- `AdditionalBeanBuildItem.builder()` exists? Yes. `setDefaultScope(DotName)`.
