Now add a test for MCP annotations and protocol. In `PathlandDevUiRpcTest`:
- `protocol("SET_TEXT")` returns rows containing SET_TEXT.
- Reflection test:
  ```java
  @Test
  void mcpExposureIsReadOnlyByDefault() throws Exception {
      Method sessions = PathlandDevUiRpc.class.getMethod("sessions");
      assertTrue(sessions.isAnnotationPresent(DevMCPEnableByDefault.class));
      assertEquals(EnumSet.of(Usage.DEV_UI, Usage.DEV_MCP), usageSet(sessions));
      Method resync = PathlandDevUiRpc.class.getMethod("resync", String.class);
      assertFalse(resync.isAnnotationPresent(DevMCPEnableByDefault.class));
      assertTrue(usageSet(resync).contains(Usage.DEV_MCP));
      Method overviewSummary = PathlandDevUiRpc.class.getMethod("overviewSummary");
      assertFalse(usageSet(overviewSummary).contains(Usage.DEV_MCP));
  }
  ```
  `JsonRpcUsage.value()` returns `Usage[]`. Import `io.quarkus.runtime.annotations.DevMCPEnableByDefault`, `JsonRpcUsage`, `Usage`; `java.lang.reflect.Method`; `java.util.EnumSet`, `Arrays`.
  - Note: `Usage.devUIandDevMCP()` returns `EnumSet<Usage>`; compare `Set.of(...)` or use `EnumSet`. `JsonRpcUsage.value()` is an array; `EnumSet.copyOf(Arrays.asList(...))`.
- `protocol("SET_TEXT")`:
